From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thierry Laurion <insurgo@riseup.net>
Date: Thu, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] soc/intel/common: log the GPIO pad lock command and result

Refs: "TPM GPIO fail" https://mkukri.xyz/2024-06-01/tpm-gpio-fail.html ; coreboot ticket #576 ; https://github.com/tlaurion/tpm-gpio-fail

Two observability gaps made a successful pad lock indistinguishable from a
silent failure:

apmc_log() is the logging helper called both before raising an APM SMI and
inside the handler to identify the command. It had no case for
APM_CNT_GPIO_LOCK, so every dedicated lock command printed
"Unknown APMC 0xcd" -- a spurious error that looked like a dispatch fault
but was only a missing label. Add the case so the command is identified.

gpio_lock_smi() only logged failure. On success it set the done latch and
returned silently, so the CBMEM console could not show that the dedicated
SMI actually locked the pads -- leaving the pre-existing finalize() path
and the dedicated command indistinguishable. Log the locked pad count at
BIOS_DEBUG.

Neither change alters behaviour; they only make the lock path visible.
---
 src/cpu/x86/smi_trigger.c                  | 3 +++
 src/soc/intel/common/block/smm/smihandler.c | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/cpu/x86/smi_trigger.c b/src/cpu/x86/smi_trigger.c
index 52c7247..8d5625e 100644
--- a/src/cpu/x86/smi_trigger.c
+++ b/src/cpu/x86/smi_trigger.c
@@ -18,6 +18,9 @@ static void apmc_log(const char *fn, u8 cmd)
 	case APM_CNT_FINALIZE:
 		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "%s: Finalizing SMM.\n", fn);
 		break;
+	case APM_CNT_GPIO_LOCK:
+		printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "%s: Locking SoC GPIO pads.\n", fn);
+		break;
 	case APM_CNT_ELOG_GSMI:
 		break;
 	case APM_CNT_SMMSTORE:
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/common/block/smm/smihandler.c b/src/soc/intel/common/block/smm/smihandler.c
index 000b95a..25fb6ae 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/common/block/smm/smihandler.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/common/block/smm/smihandler.c
@@ -373,6 +373,8 @@ static void gpio_lock_smi(void)
 		return;
 	}
 	gpio_lock_done = 1;
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "%s: SoC GPIO pads locked (%zu pad%s)\n",
+	       __func__, soc_gpio_num, soc_gpio_num == 1 ? "" : "s");
 }

 static void finalize(void)
